dzn: Keep views of mutable images within their format family without relaxed casting

Without relaxed format casting, Dozen creates a mutable-format image as a
typeless resource, and Direct3D 12 takes only views of that format family.
Vulkan allows any view format of the same texel size: an R8G8B8A8 image seen
as R32_UINT, R16G16_SFLOAT or B8G8R8A8, say. Such a view was an invalid
call, and Intel's Direct3D 12 driver under WSL2 (a UHD 770) removed the
device for it, at CreateShaderResourceView, taking down every app sharing
the device: 980 of the dEQP-VK.image.mutable cases did that there.

On such GPUs a view of another family now gets the image's own format, as
do the clears and render pass resolves Dozen makes through such views (an
integer stand-in is resolved from sample 0, as integers cannot be
averaged): the texels are read or written with the wrong type, and the
device stays. A warning says so once.

A clear through such a view writes the bits the view's format gives the
colour, and a clear Direct3D 12 cannot take as floats is not turned into a
copy into a multisampled texture, which is invalid.

